<section class="tab-pane" id="tab-runs" role="tabpanel"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>Repetition details</h2><p>Inspect every serial and concurrent phase, execution order, configuration, and raw target metadata.</p></div></div><div class="toolbar"><input class="search" id="runs-search" type="search" placeholder="Filter target details…" aria-label="Filter target details"><span class="subtitle" id="runs-count"></span></div><div class="accordions" id="run-accordions"></div></section>
<section class="tab-pane" id="tab-methodology" role="tabpanel"><div class="section-head"><div><h2>How to read this report</h2><p>The dashboard distinguishes sustainable rankings from peak observations.</p></div></div><div id="stability-notice"></div><div class="definitions" style="margin-top:15px"><article class="definition"><h3>Sustainable throughput</h3><p>Only a concurrency level whose RPM spread stays within the configured stability threshold can be ranked.</p></article><article class="definition"><h3>Peak observed throughput</h3><p>The highest median RPM seen during this run. It remains visible even when variance prevents a sustainable rank.</p></article><article class="definition"><h3>Latency percentiles</h3><p>p50, p95, and p99 cover successful validated responses. Lower values mean requests complete faster.</p></article><article class="definition"><h3>Error rate</h3><p>Failed transfers, timeouts, invalid statuses, and rejected response bodies count against the measured phase.</p></article><article class="definition"><h3>Remote telemetry</h3><p>PHP peak memory, execution time, and included files are emitted by each target and parsed separately from client latency.</p></article><article class="definition"><h3>Fairness controls</h3><p>Targets rotate execution order between repetitions and must pass response and telemetry validation before measurement.</p></article></div><article class="card" style="margin-top:16px"><div class="card-head"><div><h3 class="card-title">Recorded environment and benchmark configuration</h3><div class="subtitle">Values come from the first target; per-target variations remain available under Run details.</div></div></div><div class="config-grid" id="common-config"></div></article></section>
